Catalogs, and Resources Institutes and Centers Utica University at Florida Tuition and Fees: ABSN Program Accepted Students Current Offerings General Education Planning Sheet Themed Pathways Opportunity Programs Work closely with Superheroes. When you meet them, you’ll discover that Utica University faculty have super powers . Intellectually, they can leap tall buildings in a single bound. In the fields they teach, their practical, professional experience is as bulletproof as their academic credentials. But their most awe-inspiring attribute is this: our faculty are very easy to know and fun to work with . Before long, you’ll see them as mentors and colleagues. They will amaze you not only with their knowledge and practical expertise but also their accessibility. Most importantly, the faculty at Utica is dedicated to your success . They’re the most helpful superheroes you’ll ever meet. Meet Our Faculty: Dr. Thomas Crist, Physical Therapy The head of Utica University’s annual forensic anthropology field school in Butrint, Albania, Dr. Crist helped identify victims of the 9/11 terrorist attacks and was recently named a Top Forensic Science Professor by forensicscollege.com. More about Dr. Crist Dr. Jessica Thomas, Biology Professor Thomas’s ongoing work on cell biology is at the forefront of her field, with potential impact on the fight against cancer and other diseases. More about Dr. Thomas Dr. Gary Leising, English A published poet, Professor Leising has written two collections of his own work and in 2013 won the Brick Road Poetry Prize for his poem, “The Alp at the End of My Street”. His work has been featured on National Public Radio and in numerous literary journals. More about Dr. Leising Faculty Stories Faculty Dr. Christopher Riddle Awarded Prestigious Clark Endowed Professorship Distinguished Professor of Philosophy Dr. Christopher Riddle has been awarded the prestigious Harold T. Clark Endowed Professorship. The award is... On Campus Utica University Welcomes Jennifer Waters as Convocation Speaker Jennifer Waters ’09, G’17, vice president for business development at New York State’s Governor’s Office of Semiconductor Expansion, Management, and... Faculty Life, Death, and the Choices In-Between Faced with a challenge to its Medical Aid in Dying (MAiD) policy, the Canadian government turned to a recognized expert... All Stories Programs Financial Aid Admissions Close Window I would like to see logins and resources for: Which audience would you like to see logins and resources for? Current Undergraduate Students Current Graduate Students Current Online Students Admitted Students Parents and Families Faculty Staff Submit For a general list of frequently used logins, you can also visit our logins page . Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Academics Tuition and Financial Aid Admissions Community Athletics 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502 Map & Directions (315) 792-3006 Contact Us Institutional Effectiveness Bookstore Disability Learning Support Student Right to Know"
