      "title": "Adjunct Teaching Application",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Employment Opportunities | Utica University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics Programs Admissions Program List Tuition and Fees: Florida Programs Tuition and Fees: ABSN Program Accepted Students General Education Current Offerings Program Details Themed Pathways Planning Sheet Online Programs Online Business Programs Online Business Program Stories Honors Program Graduate Study International Ed & Study Abroad Study Abroad Semester Programs Short-Term Programs Albania / Greece Field School IPE in Ecuador IPE in Egypt IPE in Ghana London In Literature January Term Programs Study Abroad Scholarships Exceptional Faculty Research & Experiential Learning Experiential Learning Courses Student Support and Success Schedules, Catalogs, and Resources Institutes and Centers Tuition and Financial Aid Understanding Financial Aid Value Outcome Stories Excelsior, Explained University Scholarships Endowed Scholarships Annual Awards Pioneer Passport Applying For Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Utica Campus Programs Online Programs ABSN Program Graduate Campus and Online Programs Net Price Calculator Admissions First-Year Admissions Transfer Admissions Articulation Agreements Graduate Admissions Graduate Inquiry Form International Applicants International Inquiry Form Frequently Asked Questions Visit Virtual Tour Utica University Campus Why Not Fly? Apply Now Contact Us Accepted Student Info High School Counselors High School Bridge Program Community Living on Campus Res Life and Student Living Housing Selection and Requirements Important Dates Move-In Information Policies, Processes, and Forms Dining Campus Safety Residence Halls Submit a Res Hall Work Order Frequently Asked Questions Student Living Student Staff Positions Resident Assistants Microfridge Campus Engagement and Student Activities Student Organizations Clubs & Organizations Manual Leadership Programs Transportation Greek Life Satellite Locations Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (new) Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Bias Incident Reporting Community Connections DEI Collaborative DEI Awards DEI Events DEI Book Club Unity Walk Black Heritage Greek Storm Weekend More DEI Events Our Staff Resources & Trainings Pronouns Change Your Name DEI Reading Guides LACRELA Center for Career Readiness TRIO Student Support Services Opportunity Programs Young Scholars Liberty Partnerships Program Utica University Stance Statement Wilcox Center The Utica Area Hotels and Restaurants in the Utica Area Utica Stories About Utica Athletics Intercollegiate Athletics Esports News & Events Alumni Giving Apply Now Directory About Library Logins Open the search panel Search Utica University Go Click to access the searchbar Click to access the menu Adjunct Teaching Application Home Directory Adjunct Teaching Application More In This Section Click to expose navigation links on mobile. Questions? Send us an e-mail Related Links Academic Calendar Adjunct Faculty Handbook Courses Offered Additional Adjunct Information Invitation to Self Identify Equal Employment Opportunity Employment Opportunities at UC Staff/Faculty Student/Summer Employment Welcome to the Utica University Adjunct Faculty Employment Opportunities web page APPLY NOW Utica University Application Process We are currently accepting applications for adjunct instructors to teach in all disciplines to support programmatic and enrollment growth. If you hold the minimum of a master’s degree, you are welcome to submit your application for consideration. Review course descriptions Complete the online instructor application and attach your CV and unofficial transcripts for review. You will receive an auto-reply once you have successfully submitted your application. Although we are accepting applications in all disciplines we may not have an immediate need for someone with your background and experience.  Your information will stay on file and active.  If we have an opening that is a match for you, you will be contacted by a member of the Office of Human Resources. Expectation of Adjuncts Expectations for adjunct faculty at Utica University are outlined in the Adjunct Faculty Handbook . Information that is program specific will come directly from the program/department director/chair upon hire. Please be advised that if you teach any online courses, you will be responsible for ensuring that you have the correct equipment or software to fulfill your teaching responsibilities.  The University does not provide equipment or software for online adjunct assignments. Compensation and Pay Schedule Utica University offers competitive adjunct pay rates which and are determined by qualifications. Adjunct Hiring Process Once hired, a new adjunct employee will receive a packet of forms, which consist of a background check release form and new hire paperwork that need to be completed immediately.  These forms may also be found on the Human Resources website . A member of the school office (School of Heath Profession and Education or School of Business & Justice Studies or School of Arts & Sciences) will then reach out with information to set up all Utica University accounts. New adjuncts can expect to be contacted by a member of our Center for Innovative Learning for training on the Utica University LMS. New adjunct faculty will receive an invitation for orientation.  Orientation is held prior to the start of the Fall and Spring semesters. Invitations are sent by the Office of the Provost. Contact Us Office of Human Resources Office of Human Resources 124 White Hall hr@utica.edu (315) 792-3276 Close Window I would like to see logins and resources for: Which audience would you like to see logins and resources for? Current Undergraduate Students Current Graduate Students Current Online Students Admitted Students Parents and Families Faculty Staff Submit For a general list of frequently used logins, you can also visit our logins page . Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Academics Tuition and Financial Aid Admissions Community Athletics 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502 Map & Directions (315) 792-3006 Contact Us Institutional Effectiveness Bookstore Disability Learning Support Student Right to Know Processing"
    }
